.TH BOOMERANGZ.TOML 5 "September 2026" "boomerangz" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
boomerangz.toml \- boomerangz daemon configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
The primary file is read before lexically ordered
.I /etc/boomerangz/config.d/*.toml
drop-ins. Tables merge recursively, later scalar values override earlier values,
and arrays replace earlier arrays. ZFS dataset policy is not configured here;
it uses
.B org.boomerangz:*
user properties.
.SH DAEMON
The
.B [daemon]
table accepts
.BR reconcile_interval ,
.BR inactive_grace_period ,
.BR management_workers ,
.BR local_transfer_workers ,
and
.BR remote_transfer_workers .
Durations use Go duration syntax. A zero inactive grace period disables automatic
retirement. Zero management workers selects the process's available logical CPU
count.
.SH PATHS
The
.B [paths]
table accepts
.BR credentials_dir ,
.BR identity_dir ,
and
.BR socket_path .
The service account must be able to read credentials and write the identity and
socket locations.
.SH REMOTES
Each
.B [remotes.NAME]
table defines an SSH or native destination. Fields are
.BR transport ,
.BR credential ,
.BR endpoint ,
.BR host ,
.BR port ,
.BR user ,
.BR root ,
.BR identity_file ,
.BR ssh_shell_path ,
and
.BR connect_timeout .
Transport is
.B ssh
or
.BR native .
For SSH, endpoint is
.BR direct ,
.BR ssh-shell ,
or
.BR auto .
Native transport uses an imported pairing named by
.B credential
and does not accept SSH connection fields.
Strict host-key checking is always enabled.
The default
.B ssh_shell_path
is
.BR boomerangz ,
which must resolve through the remote account's command path. Set an absolute
path when the remote executable is installed elsewhere or the account uses a
restricted command path.
.SH SSH SHELL
The optional
.B [ssh_shell]
table configures the replication service exposed by the packaged
.BR boomerangz-shell
login shell.
.B replication_roots
is an array of ZFS destination roots. Every request is checked against this
server-side allow-list. An empty list disables the SSH shell service.
.SH LISTENERS
Each
.B [listeners.NAME]
table defines an optional authenticated TCP control listener. Fields are
.BR network ,
.BR address ,
.BR advertised_address ,
.BR auth_mode ,
.BR tls_cert ,
.BR tls_key ,
.BR client_ca ,
.BR pairing_ca ,
.BR pairing_pin_certificate ,
and
.BR replication_roots .
Network is
.B unix
or
.BR tcp .
TCP authentication modes are
.BR token ,
.BR mtls ,
and
.BR mtls+token .
There is no unauthenticated TCP mode.
When the TLS certificate and key are omitted, boomerangz manages a private CA
and renewable server certificate using the client-visible
.BR advertised_address .
Replication roots expose only the listed ZFS destination subtrees; an empty
list keeps a TCP listener control-only.
.SH VALIDATION
Run
.B boomerangz config check
after changing any configuration source. Run
.B boomerangz config show
to inspect the merged, redacted result.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boomerangz (1),
.BR zfsprops (7)
